WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:04.739
- I will see children feeling insecure

00:00:04.739 --> 00:00:06.495
about who they were
because of their skin color

00:00:06.495 --> 00:00:09.080
and their complexion, but I'll
also witness that children

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.485
were making fun of each other
based off of their skin color.

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:13.653
♫ Look at her hair

00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:14.890
♫ Look at her braids

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:15.914
♫ Look at her eyes

00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:18.314
♫ Look at her nose

00:00:18.314 --> 00:00:20.549
♫ Look at her fro

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:22.911
Black children, like, calling
each other, “Blackie,”

00:00:22.911 --> 00:00:25.210
saying their hair is like, nappy.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.789
I witnessed this for a long time,

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.045
so I created this song for
the children that I teach

00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:30.949
because I wanted to
change their perception

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:33.210
of beauty and how they
felt about themselves

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.683
and I want to encourage
them to love themselves.

00:00:35.683 --> 00:00:37.623
♫ My black is beautiful

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:38.760
♫ Beautiful

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.614
♫ My black is beautiful

00:00:41.614 --> 00:00:44.158
♫ My black is beautiful

00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:47.406
I remember growing up
and feeling very insecure

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:50.478
about the way I looked, I felt my nose

00:00:50.478 --> 00:00:53.198
was like not straight enough, was too flat

00:00:53.198 --> 00:00:54.904
and I felt my skin was dark.

00:00:54.904 --> 00:00:56.824
Also when you look on the television,

00:00:56.824 --> 00:00:58.723
the images that were portrayed,

00:00:58.723 --> 00:01:02.067
did not reflect who I
was as a Black child.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:05.187
After attending college,
I took a trip to Africa

00:01:05.187 --> 00:01:09.104
that really made me
embrace and love who I was.

00:01:09.995 --> 00:01:12.454
I teach at a charter school called,

00:01:12.454 --> 00:01:14.910
Helen Y. Davis Leadership Academy.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.712
We have what's called a girls' group.

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:19.060
One of the things we talk
about is, self-esteem

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.687
because I saw that many of
the young girls I taught,

00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:23.267
didn't feel good about themselves

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.367
and they felt uncomfortable
in their Black skin.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:28.846
So the do now question
is, do you know think

00:01:28.846 --> 00:01:30.627
skin color determines a person's

00:01:30.627 --> 00:01:32.926
value or worth in this society?

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.947
- I said, no because I don't think

00:01:34.947 --> 00:01:38.184
your skin should define
you in any type of way.

00:01:38.184 --> 00:01:39.931
- We have to work hard and not

00:01:39.931 --> 00:01:42.493
listen to what people
say and keep our mind

00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:44.466
focused on school so that we can make it

00:01:44.466 --> 00:01:46.478
to where we want to be.

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:48.857
- I think it's important to use music

00:01:48.857 --> 00:01:52.557
as a way to inspire and to
transform people's lives.

00:01:52.557 --> 00:01:54.377
I vowed to make this
song for all Black girls

00:01:54.377 --> 00:01:57.561
to really define beauty for themselves.

00:01:57.561 --> 00:01:59.140
♫ In life

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.558
♫ There's one thing you should remember

00:02:02.558 --> 00:02:06.725
♫ That love yourself is more
precious than anything else

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.959
I already see a lot of the young ladies

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:12.569
feeling much more confident,
they're much more outspoken

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:15.070
and they're much more willing
to tell their stories.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.329
- My Black is beautiful.

00:02:16.329 --> 00:02:17.431
- My Black is beautiful.

00:02:17.431 --> 00:02:19.332
- My Black is beautiful.

00:02:19.332 --> 00:02:21.689
- So what happens when children
feel good about themselves,

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:24.830
that transfers to all other
aspects of your lives.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.772
There are many problems
we can solve in this world

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:29.092
and mine is to make sure that Black women

00:02:29.092 --> 00:02:30.967
feel good about themselves
and Black children

00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:32.148
feel good about themselves because

00:02:32.148 --> 00:02:36.148
I think that is the
foundation of all education.

